Draft a short PR comment reply to Michael. He asked "Can you give an example of this?" on this jsdoc in apps/roam/src/components/settings/components/BlockPropSettingPanels.tsx:

  /** Legacy block text when it must differ from `title`; readers such as
   *  discourseConfigRef.ts match on it exactly. Defaults to `title`. */
  blockKey?: string;

Facts to convey: two of the three call sites have blockKey != title. (1) Node trigger: panel title is now "Graph-wide default" but the legacy block text is "trigger" — the title changed in this PR because the panel became half of the "Node trigger" group. (2) Enable left sidebar: panel title "Enable left sidebar", block text "(BETA) Left Sidebar" — pre-existing mismatch. (3) Canvas Page Format: title and blockKey are identical, so it's redundant there. The panels write `blockKey ?? title` as the block string, and getUidAndStringSetting matches that text exactly against the config tree, so renaming a UI label without blockKey would write a new block while readers keep reading the old one — the user's value would look like it reset.

